{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvquXwfrTeNvvtDRD4mK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WLUSs7kuvDEhPUbjxdYZPV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; cp paper.tex /tmp/paper_before.tex; python3 - <<'E'\nt=open('paper.tex').read()\ndef r(old,new,cnt=1):\n    global t\n    assert t.count(old)==cnt,(old,t.count(old))\n    t=t.replace(old,new)\nr(\"Refit-Verified Removal Budgets on Crowd-Vote and Sports Data\",\"Recorded Removal Budgets on Crowd-Vote and Sports Data\")\nr(\"after an exact ridge-regularised Bradley--Terry refit. We measure it\",\"under a ridge-regularised Bradley--Terry refit, as recorded by the task's evaluator. We measure it\")\nr(\"Verified budgets are small: 62\",\"Recorded budgets are small: 62\")\nr(\"Because every proposed deletion set is checked by an exact refit, any reported budget is a certificate that a reversal is attainable with that many rows, and therefore an upper bound on the true minimum.\",\n  \"The evaluator records, for each returned set, its size $k$ and a flip indicator; we could not inspect how it verifies them, so we read a recorded budget as an upper bound on the true minimum (a smaller set might exist) and rely on the evaluator's records rather than on an independent check.\")\nr(\"Under an exact BT refit (ridge $0.01$, ties as half wins)\",\"Under a BT refit as defined by the task's metric (ridge $0.01$, ties as half wins)\")\nr(\"(1) A precisely specified, evaluator-verified removal-budget protocol with comparators and controls, whose budgets are certificates rather than estimates.\",\"(1) A precisely specified removal-budget protocol with comparators and controls, whose recorded budgets are upper bounds on the true minimum; the evaluator's verification procedure was not inspectable.\")\nr(\"(i) Budgets are small in all four held-out cases\",\"(i) Recorded budgets are small in all four held-out cases\")\nr(\"We measure verified removal budgets on two held-out tables\",\"We measure recorded removal budgets on two held-out tables\")\nr(\"We accept a removal set only after an exact refit reverses the pair.\",\"The studied configuration accepts a removal set only after its own exact refit reverses the pair.\")\nr(\"Our setting is a deletion-only perturbation checked by exact refit, with no adversary model\",\"Our setting is a deletion-only perturbation with no adversary model\")\nr(\"and every set is then verified by an exact refit.\",\"and every set is then checked by the candidate's own exact refit.\")\nr(\"the evaluator records its own verified budget for the returned set.\",\"the evaluator records a budget for the returned set, and we could not inspect how it verifies it.\")\nr(\"so the returned $k$ is a verified upper bound on the minimum and minimality is not claimed.\",\"so the returned $k$ is an upper bound on the minimum and minimality is not claimed.\")\nr(\"and keeps any strictly smaller verified set.\",\"and keeps any strictly smaller set that its own refit confirms.\")\nr(\"every remaining row is a genuine observation, so a flip cannot be blamed on fabricated data, and an exact refit turns each deletion set into a checkable certificate.\",\"every remaining row is a genuine observation, so a flip cannot be blamed on fabricated data, and each deletion set is in principle checkable by refitting.\")\nr(\"the evaluator refits exactly and records the verified budget $k$ and score $1-k/\\\\kcap$.\",\"the task's metric, as we understand it, records the budget $k$ and score $1-k/\\\\kcap$ for the returned set.\")\nr(\"give the verified budgets of the studied\",\"give the recorded budgets of the studied\")\nr(\"B2 and B3 report the verified budget of each comparator.\",\"B2 and B3 report the recorded budget of each comparator.\")\nr(\"Verified removal budget as a percent\",\"Recorded removal budget as a percent\")\nr(\"Verified top-pair budget in rows\",\"Recorded top-pair budget in rows\")\nr(\"Hence the per-share contrast is largely a denominator effect for the top pairs, and in absolute rows the two designs are equally fragile there.\",\n  \"Hence the per-share contrast is largely a denominator effect for the top pairs: the studied configuration's upper bounds are the same number of rows (62) for both. True minima, and so relative fragility in rows, are not established, and the caps differ (2,713 versus 258).\")\nr(\"under one verified protocol, one adjacent top pair in each of two specific tables can be reversed by deleting 62 rows.\",\"under one recorded protocol, one adjacent top pair in each of two specific tables is recorded as reversed by deleting 62 rows.\")\nr(\"Random removal is informative here: it never flips a top pair (0 of 20 draws, in either table) or the sports mid pair, but flips the crowd mid pair in 6 of 20 draws. So the crowd mid pair is sufficiently close that undirected deletion of up to 2\\\\% of rows sometimes suffices, while an influence-ordered set needs only 4 rows. The registry does not record rating gaps, so we do not test whether smaller gaps explain this ordering.\",\n  \"Random removal is informative here: it never flips a top pair (0 of 20 draws, in either table) or the sports mid pair, but flips the crowd mid pair in 6 of 20 draws, while an influence-ordered set needs only 4 rows. This suggests, but does not establish, a small rating gap for the crowd mid pair. The registry does not record rating gaps, so we do not test whether smaller gaps explain this ordering.\")\nr(\"adjacent-pair reversals under an exact BT refit can be certified with very small deletions: at most 62 rows from tables of 12,900 and 135,630 comparisons. The certified budgets are upper bounds.\",\"adjacent-pair reversals under the studied BT objective are recorded with very small deletions: at most 62 rows from tables of 12,900 and 135,630 comparisons. The recorded budgets are upper bounds.\")\nr(\"using exact-refit verification. On two\",\"as recorded by the task's evaluator. On two\")\nr(\"the verified budgets were 62 and 4\",\"the recorded budgets were 62 and 4\")\nr(\"Every reported budget comes from the evaluator's own exact refit.\",\"Every reported budget is the evaluator's recorded value for the returned set; we could not inspect how the evaluator verifies it, and the only inspectable refit is the candidate's own.\")\nr(\"how far the certified budgets are from the minimum\",\"how far the recorded budgets are from the minimum\")\nr(\"our evaluator fixes a plain ridge-penalised BT objective\",\"the task's metric, as we understand it, fixes a plain ridge-penalised BT objective\")\nopen('paper.tex','w').write(t)\nE\ngrep -n -i \"verified\\|certif\" paper.tex | cut -c1-160"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1791,"cache_read_input_tokens":83531,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1791},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d841d41f-c000-4b60-b299-3e2d0a0a7065","uuid":"e0bdaeb6-c2ab-46a9-a9dc-c5f6ee3134c4","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:42:57.131Z","request_id":"req_011CgvquWnUn3GqJQ4odDu2m"}
